{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Only you</b> — as if to say, I knew your afflictions and I delivered you, and in return for your serving me you rebelled against me; therefore I will punish. And the correct interpretation: like the manner of <i>those near to me I sanctify myself</i>, and thus is the way of kings, to be angry at their servants who stand before them, who know their customs more than do the villagers."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:52.326797285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}